      Update tree-sitter grammars: lua (#7235)
      
      Automated grammar update for **lua**.
      
      ### lua
      
      - Changed upstream. The grammar is now maintained in the tree-sitter
      repo.
      - Lua parsing now supports Lua 5.4 variable attributes and Lua 5.5
      leading attributes, global declarations, and named vararg parameters.
      - Lua parsing now accepts Unicode identifiers, hashbang lines, and
      additional numeric forms including LuaJIT binary, LL/ULL, and imaginary
      literals.
      - Lua AST conversion now preserves elseif branches in source order,
      including when an else branch is present, and correctly retains
      member-assignment receivers and colon-method declaration names.
      - Lua string ASTs now separate single-quoted and long-bracket delimiters
      from their content, consistently with double-quoted strings. Escape
      contents remain uninterpreted.
      - Lua parsing now handles builtin names such as next as ordinary
      callable identifiers.
      - This also replaces the C++ scanner with one coded in C.
      
